  "body": "Stacked on #3353 (merge #3353 first).\n\n## What changed\n\nFace now shows the shared \"Pass starts at\" row on its Passes tab. The row is held at Auto and is disabled. A line under it, in view, says why: Face rows run edge to edge, so there is no inside or outside order.\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/pass_start_row.rs`: new `no_pass_order_row` and the text `FACE_NO_PASS_ORDER`. The row uses the same label and combo as 2D Offset.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/mill2d_page.rs`: the Face Passes tab draws that row.\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/edit.rs`: `edit_operation` with `pass_start` on a Face is refused by name. The message says that Face has no pass order and that its rows run edge to edge. Before, the refusal was the generic \"unknown field\". Every word is refused, `auto` too, because Face has no such field.\n- `site/content/guide/operations/operations-2d.md`: one row in the Face table.\n- `docs/decisions/3356-face-pass-start.md`: the decision.\n\nThe issue permits this result: \"If Face has no pass order, its row says so by name, and the issue records why.\"\n\n## Cause\n\nFace cuts serpentine rows from the low Y edge to the high Y edge (`face_over`, `band`). The first row and the last row are both at an edge. There are no rings. An Inside or Outside order has no meaning for these rows. A centre-out order would add a lift and a link through clearance for each row, with no machining gain. So Face gets no `pass_start` field. A field that changes nothing would mislead the user.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `camcraft-app` `face_pass_start::mcp_refuses_pass_start_on_face_by_the_row_order`: `outside`, `inside` and `auto` are refused with the reason, and the job does not change. Red before the fix: the message was `unknown field pass_start - a face operation has no field \"pass_start\"`.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib `egui_app::tests::pass_start::the_face_passes_tab_says_it_has_no_pass_order`: one `Pass starts at` row, one disabled combo that shows Auto, and the reason in view. Red before the fix: no row (0, expected 1).\n- `every_field_lives_on_exactly_one_section`: the Face Passes row list now has `Pass starts at` (an expected change).\n\nMutation checks (old file put back from `base-3353`, pin run, file restored):\n- `mcp/edit.rs` old: the MCP pin is red. Restored: green.\n- `mill2d_page.rs` old: the UI pin is red. Restored: green.\n\nQuick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base base-3353` (the #3353 head): 30 steps, 0 failed. It ran app lib, `face_pass_start`, `mcp_enum_patch` and the other touched app suites, and ui lib and the touched ui suites. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. Face output does not change: the planner is not touched.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No GUI screenshot was taken.\n- The heavy lanes were not run. The diff does not touch `motion` or any generator.\n- A project file with a `pass_start` key on a Face is not tested. Face writes no such key. Serde ignores an unknown key on load, as it did before.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill row for this refusal is not added. The edit of `.claude/skills/` was blocked in this session. A follow-up can add one sentence to the Pass starts at row.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3353: the stack base (`pass_start_row.rs`, `mcp/edit.rs`, `mill2d_page.rs`, `tests.rs`, the guide).\n- #3251: changes other lines of `patched()` in `mcp/edit.rs` (the back-check loop). This PR adds a guard before the merge loop. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #2890 and #2817: change other arms of `fields()` in `mill2d_page.rs`. Not the Face arm.\n- Many open PRs change `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs`. This PR changes one line of the Face table.\n\nChangelog: Face: the Passes tab shows \"Pass starts at\" as not used, with the reason (Face rows run edge to edge); MCP refuses pass_start on a Face by that reason.\n\nFixes #3356\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
